{"Inconsistent metric tag key naming: timer uses 'shards' but produce timer/segment-size metric uses 'shard', which will split metric series and complicate dashboards": 0.6638607382774353, "time.sleep(0.1) is patched to a no-op at the top of the test, so it doesn't actually wait for the flusher to observe the drift change, making the test timing-dependent/flaky on slower CI": 0.8550928831100464, "isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process) guard may not match processes created via multiprocessing.get_context('spawn').Process, causing hung children to not be killed before replacement and leaking flusher workers": 0.5762644410133362, "When timeout elapses in join(), the break exits the loop without terminating remaining flusher processes, leaving background workers running during shutdown/rebalance": 0.9061790108680725, "--flusher-processes accepts negative integers which can make SpanFlusher.num_processes invalid and crash shard-to-process mapping/modulo at startup - should enforce minimum of 1": 0.7231919169425964}